[:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "3 –  8 August 1992"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/668"} "Estadio Olímpico de Montjuïc, Barcelona"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/64031"} "51 from 40 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The heavy favorite was 1992 world champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/64305"} "Noureddine Morceli"] " but he ran a strangely passive race and finished only 7th. The final started slowly, with nobody wanting to take the lead. The bell was passed in 2:49.7, with Kenya’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/72749"} "Joseph Chesire"] " leading, after 800 had been passed in a pedestrian 2:06.83. Morceli was trapped in the pack and never challenged. Spain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/67175"} "Fermín Cacho"] " saw a small gap on the inside and took the lead 250 metres from the finish. He pulled away and won over " [:a {:href "/athletes/73316"} "Rachid El-Basir"] " quite easily, looking around frequently on the final stretch. " [:a {:href "/athletes/75091"} "Mohamed Sulaiman"] "’s medal was the first ever for Qatar in the Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "404"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67175"} "Fermín Cacho"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] [:td {} "3:37.04 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:34.93 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "3:40.12 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1205"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/73316"} "Rachid El-Basir"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/co